## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design a robust, auditable CAPA for external data sources, focusing on provenance, containment speed, and reproducibility of fixes in a multi-source pipeline.

## Key Concepts

- External data provenance and signatures
- Drift detection and automated containment
- CAPA data model: evidence, lineage, owners
- Metrics for containment, recurrence, and verification
- RCA templates and canary rollback planning

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: verify feed signature before ingestion
function verifySignature(feedPayload, signature, key) {
  const h = crypto.createHmac('sha256', key);
  h.update(feedPayload);
  return h.digest('hex') === signature;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle revocation of compromised feeds without delaying normal ingestion?
- What audits or reports would you expose to satisfy regulatory or governance needs?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design end-to-end CAPA workflow for data privacy policy failures, including evidence capture and cross-tenant rollout.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data modeling for evidence and artifacts
- Lifecycle state machine and ownership
- Minimal REST API design with linked logs/traces
- Tenant/region metrics for containment and recurrence
- RCA templates and canary rollout planning

## Code Example

```javascript
// CAPA core types (overview)
interface CAPA {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  evidence: string[];
  artifacts: string[];
  state: 'detected'|'triaged'|'in_progress'|'contained'|'closed';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt?: string;
  links?: { type: string; url: string }[];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale CAPA data stores across regions?
- How to ensure regulatory auditability and evidence integrity?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical CAPA design for data segregation issues in multi-tenant exports, focusing on traceability and measurable containment.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model
- Lifecycle state machine
- Minimal REST API design
- Metrics to prove effectiveness
- RCA templates and canary-based remediation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express route to create CAPA
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
let caps = [];
app.post('/caps', (req,res)=>{ const cap = req.body; cap.id = cap.id || String(Date.now()); caps.push(cap); res.status(201).json(cap);});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you store and attach evidence files?
- How would you enforce tenant isolation in the API and data store?
